+      "text": "ask;\\nthis transfers it to another model.\\n\\nSide effects: writes a handoff record via\\nai.agent_dispatch.handoff_task; updates assignee on the task.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"task_id\":{\"description\":\"Existing task id from delimit_agent_dispatch. Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"to_model\":{\"description\":\"Explicit target worker \u2014 \\\"claude\\\", \\\"codex\\\", \\\"gemini\\\", or \\\"copilot\\\". Copilot identifies a harness, not a model family. Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"context\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Notes for the next model.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"task_id\",\"to_model\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Handoff\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_agent_poll\",\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Poll\",\"description\":\"Read a tracked worker's output without inference (explicit poll).\\n\\nWhen to use: after delimit_agent_dispatch with launch starts a\\nmuse worker, to check whether it finished. Call it explicitly \u2014\\nthere is no polling loop in the server. A finished worker\\nexposes its final text here; a worker that died mid-run (e.g.\\nmodel stream idle timeout) surfaces as \\\"uncertain\\\", never as a\\nsilent completion. When the final text carries a QUESTION: block\\nfrom the worker, this call binds it to the task with a handoff\\nreceipt \u2014 answer it with delimit_agent_answer.\\nWhen NOT to use: to read audit-only dispatches (use\\ndelimit_agent_status), to close a task (use\\ndelimit_agent_complete), or in a tight loop \u2014 one explicit call\\nper check; the worker transcript is re-read each time.\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_agent_status reads the stored task\\nrecord without touching worker output; this reads the worker's\\nJSONL transcript and advances running \u2192 completed/uncertain.\\ndelimit_agent_complete accepts and closes; delimit_agent_cancel\\naborts.\\n\\nSide effects: reads the worker's JSONL transcript plus its rc\\nsidecar (no model inference) and writes the observed outcome to\\nthe task record via ai.agent_dispatch.poll_worker, with an audit\\nentry per call. Recording a worker QUESTION: block additionally\\ncreates a handoff receipt addressed to the lease owner.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"task_id\":{\"description\":\"Task id of a launched worker (AGT-xxx). Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"task_id\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Poll\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_agent_answer\",\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Answer\",\"description\":\"Answer a bound worker question and resume its muse session.\\n\\nWhen to use: after delimit_agent_poll binds a worker QUESTION:\\nblock (question_id + receipt_id) to the task. The lead answers\\nroutine technical questions directly (owner_backed=False); only\\npass owner_backed=True when the answer carries a reserved owner\\ndecision. For muse workers the SAME session is resumed with the\\nanswer as its prompt file, so question \u2192 answer \u2192 task stays\\nbound even if the lead process was replaced.\\nWhen NOT to use: to ask the worker something new (that is a\\nfresh dispatch), to close the task (use delimit_agent_complete),\\nor to abort the worker (use delimit_agent_cancel). Do not answer\\ntwice \u2014 the backend rejects a second answer to the same\\nquestion_id.\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_agent_poll surfaces the question;\\nthis resolves it. delimit_agent_status shows the waiting\\nquestion and its receipt; delimit_agent_complete closes the\\ntask after the resumed worker finishes.\\n\\nSide effects: persists the answer on the question record\\n(owner_backed recorded exactly as given, never inferred),\\nacknowledges the question's handoff receipt with the answer\\ntext, and \u2014 for muse tasks whose worker already reached\\ncompleted/uncertain \u2014 resumes the SAME session via the\\ncontained launcher with the answer as the prompt file (a fresh\\noutput prefix per resume; prior transcripts preserved). No\\nrelaunch happens while the worker is still running.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"task_id\":{\"description\":\"Task id carrying the bound question (AGT-xxx). Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"question_id\":{\"description\":\"Question id from delimit_agent_poll (Q-xxx). Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"answer\":{\"description\":\"Answer text for the worker. Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"owner_backed\":{\"default\":false,\"description\":\"If True, the answer carries an owner decision. Default False (routine lead answer).\",\"type\":\"boolean\"}},\"required\":[\"task_id\",\"question_id\",\"answer\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Answer\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_agent_cancel\",\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Cancel\",\"description\":\"Cancel a task and terminate its worker process if still alive.\\n\\nWhen to use: to withdraw delegated work \u2014 a stuck or misguided\\nworker, a duplicate dispatch, or a task the plan no longer\\nneeds. Records \\\"cancelled\\\" with the reason and signals the live\\nworker (pid recorded at launch, cmdline-validated against the\\nsession id, with a pkill-by-session fallback). Cancellation and\\n\\\"uncertain outcome\\\" stay distinct: cancelled tasks can never be\\nclosed via delimit_agent_complete \u2014 re-dispatch instead.\\nWhen NOT to use: to close finished work (use\\ndelimit_agent_complete), to read state (use\\ndelimit_agent_status), or to transfer ownership (use\\ndelimit_agent_handoff).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_agent_complete accepts and closes;\\nthis withdraws. delimit_agent_poll observes without changing\\nthe worker; this stops it.\\n\\nSide effects: writes the cancellation via\\nai.agent_dispatch.cancel_task (status, reason, timestamp, and\\nwhether a live process was signalled) plus an audit entry, and\\nreleases any checkout lock the task holds.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"task_id\":{\"description\":\"Task id to cancel (AGT-xxx). Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"reason\":{\"description\":\"Why the task is cancelled. Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"task_id\",\"reason\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Cancel\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_agent_link\",\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Link\",\"description\":\"Link an agent task to a ledger item so the dashboard shows the relationship.\\n\\nWhen to use: after delimit_agent_dispatch creates a task and you\\nwant the dashboard to show which ledger item it's working on.\\nWhen NOT to use: to dispatch a new task (delimit_agent_dispatch)\\nor close out a task (delimit_agent_complete).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_agent_dispatch creates;\\ndelimit_ledger_link links between two ledger items;\\nthis links a task to a ledger item.\\n\\nSide effects: writes the link via\\nai.agent_dispatch.link_ledger_item.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"task_id\":{\"description\":\"Agent task id (AGT-xxx). Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"ledger_item_id\":{\"description\":\"Ledger item id (LED-xxx or STR-xxx). Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"task_id\",\"ledger_item_id\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Link\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_agent_dashboard\",\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Dashboard\",\"description\":\"View the multi-agent orchestration dashboard.\\n\\nWhen to use: as a one-shot read of all agent activity grouped by\\nassignee/status \u2014 useful for orchestrator status reporting.\\nWhen NOT to use: for a single task's status (use\\ndelimit_agent_status) or to dispatch new work\\n(delimit_agent_dispatch).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_agent_status returns raw records;\\nthis returns an aggregated dashboard view.\\n\\nSide effects: read-only. Calls ai.agent_dispatch.get_agent_dashboard.\\n\\nArgs:\\n    None.\\n\\nReturns:\\n    Dict with grouped tasks, handoff history, linked ledger items,\\n    recent audit trail, next_steps.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Dashboard\",\"readOnlyHint\":true,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":true},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_control\",\"title\":\"Delimit Control\",\"description\":\"Aggregate all governance lanes into one queue; approve/reject approvals (LED-1709).\\n\\nWhen to use: as the shared queue the CLI and web dashboard both render \u2014\\nattestations, approvals, sensing (STR-*), ops (LED-*) \u2014 and to\\napprove/reject founder-approval items from that same surface.\\nWhen NOT to use: to act on attestation/sensing/ops items; approve/reject\\nare approval-class only in Phase 1 (mutate those via their owning tool).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_agent_dashboard is dispatch-only,\\ndelimit_ledger_context is one-venture-only, delimit_notify_inbox is\\ninbox-only; this unifies all four into one lane-aware view.\\n\\nSide effects: list/get are READ-ONLY. approve/reject append the same\\n`founder_directive_completed` ack the email \\\"ship it\\\" loop writes to the\\nEXISTING store (~/.delimit/inbox_routing.jsonl); reject stamps\\ndisposition=\\\"rejected\\\". No new store; idempotent re-approve no-ops.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"action\":{\"default\":\"list\",\"description\":\"\\\"list\\\" (default), \\\"get\\\", \\\"approve\\\", or \\\"reject\\\". list/get are read-only; approve/reject act ONLY on approval-class items and mirror the email \\\"ship it\\\" ack loop.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"class_filter\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Lane filter: \\\"\\\" (all), \\\"attestation\\\", \\\"approval\\\", \\\"sensing\\\", or \\\"ops\\\".\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"state_filter\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"State filter, e.g. \\\"open\\\", \\\"pending\\\", \\\"awaiting_approval\\\", \\\"done\\\". \\\"\\\" = all.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"item_id\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Required for \\\"get\\\", \\\"approve\\\", \\\"reject\\\": the normalized item id (e.g. \\\"att_\u2026\\\", \\\"STR-437\\\", \\\"LED-1709\\\", \\\"WO-\u2026\\\", \\\"DIR-\u2026\\\").\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"limit\":{\"default\":100,\"description\":\"Max items for action=\\\"list\\\" (default 100).\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"note\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Optional note recorded as the ack result for action=\\\"approve\\\"/\\\"reject\\\".\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Control\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":true},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_agent_policy\",\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Policy\",\"description\":\"Set or view per-model governance permissions.\\n\\nWhen to use: to inspect or modify the access policy that gates\\neach AI model's operations on the ledger, memory, evidence,\\ndeploy, and secrets.\\nWhen NOT to use: for runtime governance evaluation (use\\ndelimit_gov_evaluate) or session policy\\n(delimit_project_config).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_gov_evaluate evaluates one action;\\nthis configures the per-model policy that those evaluations use.\\n\\nSide effects: providing any of ledger/memory/deploy/evidence/\\nsecrets/custom_constraints writes via\\nai.agent_policy.set_agent_policy. Empty/no-changes is read-only.\\n\\nAccess levels for ledger/memory/evidence: \\\"read-only\\\",\\n\\\"read-write\\\", \\\"none\\\".\\nBoolean flags for deploy/secrets: \\\"true\\\" or \\\"false\\\".\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"model\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"AI model name \u2014 \\\"claude\\\", \\\"codex\\\", \\\"gemini\\\", \\\"cursor\\\". Empty = list all.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"ledger\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Ledger access level.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"memory\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Memory access level.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"deploy\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Allow deploys (\\\"true\\\"/\\\"false\\\").\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"evidence\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Evidence access level.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"secrets\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Allow secret access (\\\"true\\\"/\\\"false\\\").\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"custom_constraints\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Comma-separated constraints, e.g. \\\"no-deploy,no-publish\\\".\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Policy\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_agent_check\",\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Check\",\"description\":\"Check if a model is allowed to perform an action under agent policy.\\n\\nWhen to use: as a per-action gate before executing sensitive\\noperations from a non-orchestrator model \u2014 verify it has the\\nrequired permission.\\nWhen NOT to use: to set / inspect policies overall (use\\ndelimit_agent_policy) or for runtime governance evaluation\\n(delimit_gov_evaluate).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_agent_policy manages the policy;\\ndelimit_gov_evaluate is the runtime governance gate;\\nthis is a per-action permission check.\\n\\nSide effects: read-only on the policy store. Calls\\nai.agent_policy.check_agent_permission.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"model\":{\"description\":\"AI model name \u2014 \\\"claude\\\", \\\"codex\\\", \\\"gemini\\\", \\\"cursor\\\". Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"action\":{\"description\":\"Action to check (e.g. \\\"ledger_write\\\", \\\"deploy\\\"). Required.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"model\",\"action\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Agent Check\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_next_task\",\"title\":\"Delimit Next Task\",\"description\":\"Get the next task to work on with safeguard checks.\\n\\nWhen to use: inside a loop session, to fetch the highest-priority\\nopen task with safeguard checks (cost cap, error threshold).\\nWhen NOT to use: to mark a task done (use delimit_task_complete)\\nor list all tasks (delimit_ledger_list).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_task_complete closes + advances;\\ndelimit_ledger_list is general listing; this is the loop fetch\\nthat may return STOP.\\n\\nSide effects: read-only on the ledger. Returns action: BUILD,\\nCONSENSUS (queue empty), or STOP (safeguard tripped).\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"venture\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Project name or path. Empty = auto-detect.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"max_risk\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Max risk level \u2014 \\\"low\\\", \\\"medium\\\", \\\"high\\\", \\\"critical\\\".\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"session_id\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Resume existing session. Empty = new.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Next Task\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_ledger_propose\",\"title\":\"Delimit Ledger Propose\",\"description\":\"Propose new ledger items based on signals, completed work, and gaps.\\n\\nWhen to use: at the end of a build loop or when the queue is empty,\\nto suggest 3-5 next items with rationale.\\nWhen NOT to use: to add a known item (use delimit_ledger_add) or\\nlist current items (delimit_ledger_list).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_ledger_add commits chosen items;\\nthis proposes candidates.\\n\\nSide effects: read-only analysis (does NOT auto-create ledger\\nitems). The caller decides which proposals to commit.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"venture\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Focus on a specific venture. Empty = auto-detect.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"focus\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Optional area filter \u2014 \\\"outreach\\\", \\\"engineering\\\", \\\"security\\\", etc.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"max_items\":{\"default\":5,\"description\":\"Maximum proposals. Default 5.\",\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Ledger Propose\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_task_complete\",\"title\":\"Delimit Task Complete\",\"description\":\"Mark current loop task done and get the next one.\\n\\nWhen to use: at the end of each loop iteration \u2014 records\\ncompletion, updates session metrics, returns the next task.\\nWhen NOT to use: to close a regular ledger item (use\\ndelimit_ledger_done) or fetch next task without closing\\n(delimit_next_task).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_ledger_done is per-item;\\ndelimit_next_task only fetches; this completes + advances.\\n\\nSide effects: writes status to the ledger, updates session\\nmetrics (cost, errors), returns next task. Loop continues until\\na STOP signal.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"task_id\":{\"description\":\"Ledger item id completed (e.g. \\\"LED-042\\\").\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"result\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Summary of what was done.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"cost_incurred\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Estimated cost (USD).\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"error\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"If task failed, describe error.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"session_id\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Loop session to update.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"venture\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Project name or path.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"task_id\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Task Complete\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_loop_status\",\"title\":\"Delimit Loop Status\",\"description\":\"Check autonomous loop metrics for a session.\\n\\nWhen to use: to inspect a continuous-loop session's run-time\\nmetrics \u2014 iterations completed, cost, errors, safeguard status.\\nWhen NOT to use: to configure the loop (use delimit_loop_config)\\nor run it (delimit_build_loop).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_loop_config sets policy;\\ndelimit_build_loop runs; this reports the result.\\n\\nSide effects: read-only. Calls ai.loop_engine.loop_status.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"session_id\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Session id to check. Empty = most recent session.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Loop Status\",\"readOnlyHint\":true,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":true},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_loop_config\",\"title\":\"Delimit Loop Config\",\"description\":\"Configure autonomous build loop safeguards.\\n\\nWhen to use: BEFORE starting a loop session \u2014 to set max iterations,\\ncost cap, error threshold, approval policy.\\nWhen NOT to use: to read loop metrics (use delimit_loop_status) or\\ndrive the loop (delimit_build_loop).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_loop_status reads metrics;\\ndelimit_build_loop runs; this configures the policy.\\n\\nSide effects: writes the loop session config via\\nai.loop_engine.loop_config. Only non-zero/non-empty values are\\napplied \u2014 pass just the fields you want to change.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"session_id\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Session to configure. Empty = create new.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"max_iterations\":{\"default\":0,\"description\":\"Max tasks before stopping. Default 50.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"cost_cap\":{\"default\":0.0,\"description\":\"Max session cost in dollars. Default 5.0.\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"auto_consensus\":{\"default\":false,\"description\":\"If True, suggest consensus when ledger empty.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"error_threshold\":{\"default\":0,\"description\":\"Consecutive errors before circuit-breaker trips. Default 3.\",\"type\":\"integer\"},\"status\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Set loop status \u2014 \\\"running\\\", \\\"paused\\\", \\\"stopped\\\".\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"require_approval_for\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Comma-separated action types requiring human approval.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Loop Config\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_toolcard_cache\",\"title\":\"Delimit Toolcard Cache\",\"description\":\"Manage the tool-schema cache to reduce per-session token waste.\\n\\nWhen to use: when an MCP client repeatedly dumps full tool\\ndefinitions and you want to send only diffs across sessions.\\nWhen NOT to use: as a runtime tool dispatcher \u2014 this is a cache\\nside-channel, not a tool-call surface.\\n\\nSibling contrast: this caches tool schemas;\\ndelimit_help describes individual tools at runtime.\\n\\nSide effects: action=\\\"register\\\" /\\n\\\"clear\\\" / \\\"flush\\\" mutate the cache; \\\"status\\\" / \\\"delta\\\" /\\n\\\"estimate\\\" are read-only.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"action\":{\"default\":\"status\",\"description\":\"One of \\\"status\\\" (default), \\\"register\\\", \\\"delta\\\", \\\"clear\\\", \\\"estimate\\\", \\\"flush\\\", \\\"usage\\\" (durable tool utilization + dormancy report).\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"tool_schemas\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}],\"default\":null,\"description\":\"JSON array of tool schema objects (for register/ estimate).\"},\"tool_names\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}],\"default\":null,\"description\":\"Comma-separated tool names (for delta).\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Toolcard Cache\",\"readOnlyHint\":true,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":true},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_handoff_create\",\"title\":\"Delimit Handoff Create\",\"description\":\"Create a handoff receipt when transitioning between agents.\\n\\nWhen to use: at the end of a session or before passing work to\\nanother model \u2014 documents what was done, what's pending, and what\\nthe next agent should do first.\\nWhen NOT to use: for general session summary (use\\ndelimit_session_handoff) or to acknowledge a receipt\\n(delimit_handoff_acknowledge).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_session_handoff is venture-scoped\\nsummary; delimit_soul_capture is richer cross-model state;\\nthis is the structured per-agent handoff with explicit completed/\\nnot-completed/blockers/scope fields.\\n\\nSide effects: writes a new handoff receipt via\\nai.handoff_receipts.create_receipt. The receiving agent should\\nlater call delimit_handoff_acknowledge.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"task_description\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"What the task was (one line).\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"completed\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Comma-separated completed items.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"not_completed\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Comma-separated items not completed (with reasons).\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"assumptions\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Comma-separated assumptions made.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"blockers\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Comma-separated blockers encountered.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"files_modified\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"JSON list of {path, change_type, summary} dicts, or empty to auto-detect.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"in_scope\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Comma-separated in-scope items.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"out_of_scope\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Comma-separated explicitly excluded items.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"next_action\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"First thing the receiving agent should do.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"priority\":{\"default\":\"P1\",\"description\":\"P0 / P1 (default) / P2.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"to_model\":{\"default\":\"any\",\"description\":\"Target model name or \\\"any\\\" (default).\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Handoff Create\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_handoff_acknowledge\",\"title\":\"Delimit Handoff Acknowledge\",\"description\":\"Acknowledge a pending handoff receipt before starting work.\\n\\nWhen to use: at session start when delimit_handoff_list shows a\\npending receipt \u2014 the receiving agent must acknowledge before\\nstarting work.\\nWhen NOT to use: to create a handoff (use delimit_handoff_create)\\nor list receipts (delimit_handoff_list).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_handoff_create writes;\\ndelimit_handoff_list reads;\\nthis closes the loop on a specific receipt.\\n\\nSide effects: writes an acknowledgement record via\\nai.handoff_receipts.acknowledge_receipt; flips the receipt status\\nfrom pending to acknowledged.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"receipt_id\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Receipt id to acknowledge. Required (empty string returns an error payload).\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"notes\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Optional notes from the receiving agent.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"project_path\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Optional exact project namespace. Blank searches all namespaces; an explicit path never writes outside that namespace.\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Handoff Acknowledge\",\"readOnlyHint\":false,\"destructiveHint\":false},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}},{\"name\":\"delimit_handoff_list\",\"title\":\"Delimit Handoff List\",\"description\":\"List session handoff receipts.\\n\\nWhen to use: at session start to see what previous sessions left\\npending, or to audit acknowledged handoffs.\\nWhen NOT to use: to create a handoff (use delimit_handoff_create)\\nor acknowledge one (delimit_handoff_acknowledge).\\n\\nSibling contrast: delimit_handoff_create writes;\\ndelimit_handoff_acknowledge closes; this reads the receipt list.\\n\\nSide effects: read-only. Calls ai.handoff_receipts.get_receipts.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"status\":{\"default\":\"pending\",\"description\":\"\\\"pending\\\" (default), \\\"acknowledged\\\", or \\\"all\\\".\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"project_path\":{\"default\":\"\",\"description\":\"Optional exact project namespace. Blank aggregates all namespaces.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"limit\":{\"default\":50,\"description\":\"Maximum receipts to return, 1-200. Default 50.\",\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"outputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":true,\"type\":\"object\"},\"annotations\":{\"title\":\"Delimit Handoff List\",\"readOnlyHint\":true,\"destructiveHint\":false,\"idempotentHint\":true},\"_meta\":{\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}}}]}}\n"
+    }
+  ]
+}
